{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489468-travelling-between-pocket-dimensions","id":1489468,"title":"Travelling between pocket dimensions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-08T04:32:07-07:00","id":1489468,"title":"Travelling between pocket dimensions","content":"For story purposes, players will get sucked into a pocket dimension that mimics the real world down to a T. <br /> <br /> Meta wise, what setup would an npc need to pull this off. And what would a player need in order to hop in/out. <br /> <br /> This also includes other supernaturals from WoD. So if there powers can cross over or detect such shinnanrgans that\u2019s something I wanna make sure I\u2019m validating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T07:27:16-07:00","id":1489482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pnizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489468-travelling-between-pocket-dimensions#post1489468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For story purposes, players will get sucked into a pocket dimension that mimics the real world down to a T. <br /> <br /> Meta wise, what setup would an npc need to pull this off. And what would a player need in order to hop in/out. <br /> <br /> This also includes other supernaturals from WoD. So if there powers can cross over or detect such shinnanrgans that\u2019s something I wanna make sure I\u2019m validating.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this &quot;Alternate Earth&quot; is close enough as to not arise suspicious, I think that it would hardly be noticed as being a forgery. Few would even have a reason to try to use some specific &quot;vodoo&quot; to try to discern it.<br /> <br /> Even those that do have some sort of &quot;super power&quot; of precognition, would probably get their &quot;spider sense&quot; tingling, but wouldnt know why. Vampires with Auspex would get the felling that &quot;something is off&quot;, but unless it's Auspex 9 or 10 they wouldnt have any chance to figuring out that they are on the &quot;wrong Earth&quot;. Some gifts from the shapeshifters could also have the same results. Mages with Entropy 1 could also tell that &quot;something isnt right&quot;, but wouldnt be able to tell what.<br /> <br /> To hope in and out of it, a Mage would still only need Spirit 3, and Shapeshifters still have it as a natural ability. It would probably be hard to return to the real Earth thou, since the cosmological &quot;maps&quot; would be completely off (this would be the first sign that &quot;something is VERY wrong&quot;). You would need to know your &quot;way in&quot; to reach such an alternate Earth (and likewise, also know your way out back to the &quot;true&quot; Earth), otherwise you may end up lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T16:18:09-07:00","id":1489510,"title":"","content":"With regards to what an NPC would need to set this up:<br /> To make a whole alternate Earth would require Godlike power. In terms of Mage, this would maybe require most of the spheres at 5 and a truly absurd amount of successes. [Edit: and even then it might fail to replicate certain supernatural things unless the mage is truly deeply knowledgeabe and able to draw upon &quot;other Powers&quot; such as the powers of the celestines, the wurm, etc.]<br /> More likely though, this alternate Earth could be something that was discovered in the umbra.<br /> or else something that came to be metaphysically &quot;nearby&quot; perhaps due to some sort of Paradox Backlash of epic proportions.<br /> <br /> Dragging people to some specific part off the Umbra may require Spirit 4 and Correspondence 4<br /> Pulling people into some weird &quot;near-Earth&quot; anomaly might only require Corrspondence 4 or Spirit 4, or it might need both, depending on what its relation to Earth is exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 08-11-2022, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T21:47:20-07:00","id":1489529,"title":"","content":"There are three options to the Alternate Earth, to add to/expand on what Spacecat wrote:<br /> <br /> 1) The antagonist is very powerful in Spirit and Correspondence: A location in the High Umbra. After all, it is the infinite tapestry, where any kind of world might be found. Problem: It might be easily noticable, as none of the Magickal things you have left or set up in the original would be there, and the protagonist's Spirit/Corr senses might be yelling at them.<br /> <br /> 2) The antagonist is very powerful in Time and Correspondence: More subtle to Mage-senses: An alternate Timeline they were shifted to. It could have one miniscule change in Events that (For Plot Reasons) could be detected by the Mages and, after some more investigation make them realize they are, in fact, in an alternate Timeline and need to get back. Downside: Getting back to your OG Timeline without a temporal anchor is normally pretty impossible, but hey, the bad guy probably visited this Timeline and might have forgotten to remove (or intentionally left for further visits) the anchor in the original one...time to find something they left in the alternate Timeline to make a sympathetic connection.<br /> <br /> 3) The anagonist is very very powerful in Mind: It's all a mind-maze, but the antagonist made a mistake. Instead of trappening them in said mind-maze in an awake (but immobile) state, they did so while the protagonists are asleep, thus shunting this whole illusion-world into the dream-realm Maya by mistake instead of just the protagonist's minds. The difference? Magick actually works outside the antagonist's control in the Maya...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T01:12:11-07:00","id":1489537,"title":"","content":"I had a somewhat similar scenario for a past Hunter group, but the cause was a Marauder whose (very subtle) alternate reality bubble encompassed a whole city. So this was much more localized, and escaping was as easy as taking down the antagonist.<br /> <br /> Another way to create a huge alternate reality (and much easier than crafting a 'proper' umbral Realm) is dreamcrafting. If you think of it, your mind can easily set up most of the scenery, so if the antagonist is a skilled dreamcrafter they could create what would effectively be a Demesne, where they have godlike control. If they allow 'visitors' limited projection, the PCs would be able to subconsciously fill in the blanks for anything only they could know and not get tipped off outright. Dreams also allow for all kinds of weird things to happen to leave as clues for the PCs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T10:23:12-07:00","id":1489649,"title":"","content":"Or you could simply use the Mirror Zone. It's already established as an &quot;alternate reality&quot; where one needs to discover the discrepancy to escape. In my model of the WOD cosmology, I have akin to the 'Near Realms' of the Middle Umbra, a possible iteration of reality based on what was and could be. An antagonist could have set up an instance to send someone there, or it could be by accident and the antagonist is just exploiting the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T21:46:38-07:00","id":1489716,"title":"","content":"Checking for monkey wrenches:<br /> One player picked temporis for his vampire character. <br /> One character also picked time sense merit and eidetic memory. <br /> One can contact demonic entities for info. (I could omit this cause they could be assholes about it and not let the player know as a cruel joke.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}